  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 AM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nDrier conditions will prevail over South Texas through the early \npart of next week thanks to ridging aloft. Warmer conditions will \nalso exist through this period with highs in the 80s and 90s across \nthe region with heat indices around 100-105. This will also prevail \nthrough early next week. This will lead to minor to moderate heat \nstress conditions. \n\nThe chances for showers and storms will return to the region next \nweek as the ridge weakens allowing for some shortwave energy to \ncreep into the region which will combine with the seabreeze. Chances \nremain low to medium at this time through the remainder of the week.",
